# Claim: an open file handle held anywhere inside a value (an Option field, an Option local, an Option of a struct, a list of Options, a list, an enum payload) closes when the value's owner ends, on o0, o1 and o2; a handle moved out of an Option payload has exactly one owner and stays readable after the Option's owner ends.
# Hand-derived: each "leaked" line is the process's open descriptor count minus the count before any handle opened, so 0 means every handle the owner held closed with it; "moved open 1" is the one moved handle still open, and it closes when its new owner ends ("moved leaked 0").
fixture: handle_in_an_optional_closes_with_its_owner.fixture
env: NO_COLOR=1
env: JET_STORE_DIR={work}/cache
step: jet run --allow=FS.Read --optimize=none run.jet
exit: 0 # o0
stdout: = handle_in_an_optional_closes_with_its_owner.out # o0
step: jet run --allow=FS.Read --optimize=basic run.jet
exit: 0 # o1
stdout: = handle_in_an_optional_closes_with_its_owner.out # o1
step: jet run --allow=FS.Read --optimize=full run.jet
exit: 0 # o2
stdout: = handle_in_an_optional_closes_with_its_owner.out # o2
